#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A speed target can be calculated along a path while attempting to remain within specified target limits of lateral and longitudinal acceleration.
#
#This example uses the Speed (Closed Loop) using Path Preview to calculate a target speed profile subject to target limits of 0.7 G longitudinal and 0.3 G lateral acceleration.
#
#It enters the test section at 120 km/h, brakes hard, steers through the double lane change, then begins to accelerate.
#
#This example is overlaid with a similar run that uses a constant target speed of 48 km/h.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

